//
// PROBE: the csv conditional (Bund/src/stdlib/functions/conditional/conditional_csv.rs:9-173).
//
// csv pushes a conditional naming the file; ! runs it. Each row reaches the
// lambda as a list typed by polars' inference: `score` is integers with one
// empty cell, `active` is booleans in mixed case, `ratio` mixes integers and
// floats, so it is floats. An empty cell is null, and a null is left out of
// its row (:144). With `column`, the lambda runs once on that column's cells.
// With is_header false, the header row is data, and every column mixes kinds,
// so every column is strings.
//
"probe: each row, typed" println
"tests/probes/data/scores.csv" csv :lambda { println } set !
"probe: one column, once" println
"tests/probes/data/scores.csv" csv :column "ratio" set :lambda { println } set !
"probe: no header, so every column is strings" println
"tests/probes/data/scores.csv" csv :is_header false set :lambda { println } set !
